    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d306">

                <pb facs="0414" n="294" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg294"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Lorillard to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-12-08"><hi rendition="#italic">December 8,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 54.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform the Department
                    that a general treaty of arbitration between Denmark and Spain was signed at
                    Madrid on the 1st instant.</p>
                <p>The text of this treaty has not yet been made public. The minister of foreign
                    affairs was kind enough to tell me, however, that it is identical with that of
                    the Anglo-Danish, reported in my dispatch No. 46, of the 25th ultimo, the
                    Anglo-French, and the Anglo-Italian arbitration treaties.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">George L.
                    Lorillard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
